      "problem": "Complete the following reasoning about the set $S=(-3,\\infty ):$\n\nThe value $20$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because {{field-1}} and yet {{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if \n\n- ${x}_{max}\\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nIn our case, the value $20$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because, for example, $21\\in S$ and yet $21>20.$",
